I like most of the above ideas if they're implemented in ways *other*
than decoration, ie. you can interact with them.

Broken weapons - a whole new subclass of ineffective weaponry.  They can
still end up welded to your hand (so cursed daggers would no longer be a
reliable lockpick), and you can also hurt yourself picking them up.
Although I can't see what *advantage* they'd be, beyond silly conduct
games/ways to split puddings/another item with which to take on Vlad.

A sarcophagus could work like a tomb, wrt disturbing the undead and
finding some treasure, except with the chance of a human mummy being
released.  (This YANI has come up before.)

Shafts of light: similar effect to wand/scroll/spell of light, an
inexplicable bright patch in the middle of a dark room.  Could coincide
with falling rock traps on shallow levels ("The ceiling caves in and you
can see daylight.").

Mist - blocks visibility like (stinking) clouds.

Rubble in the corner:  See under "falling rock traps" (and also
under falling rock traps).

Skeletons?  Nethack already has them - they're monsters.  Go and play
crawl if you want the inanimate type :-p

